        </div>
        <div class="cam-why__stat-divider"></div>
        <div class="cam-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>72–74% summer humidity</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cam-why__content">
      <div class="cam-why__eyebrow">South Jersey Climate &amp; Context</div>
      <h2 class="cam-why__headline">Why Camden Needs Window Film</h2>
      <p class="cam-why__intro">Three conditions unique to Camden make window film less of an upgrade and more of a practical necessity. Summer heat regularly pushes past 88°F with 72–74% humidity. The <a href="https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/dsr/urban-heat-island-camden-rps-2004.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#7CB342">NJ Department of Environmental Protection formally identified Camden as an urban heat island</a> — dense brick and asphalt amplifying temperatures well beyond surrounding suburbs. And with one of New Jersey’s highest crime rates, security film is one of our most-requested installs here.</p>
      <ul class="cam-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Summer highs of 88–94°F with 72–74% humidity make south- and west-facing glass uncomfortable and costly without solar control film
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          Camden’s urban heat island effect — documented by the NJ DEP — means buildings absorb and retain more heat than surrounding communities
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          A <a href="https://www.neighborhoodscout.com/nj/camden/crime" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#7CB342">crime rate of 45 per 1,000 residents per NeighborhoodScout</a> (sourced from FBI data) makes security and anti-smash film one of the highest-ROI installs we do in Camden
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cam-why__climate-facts">
        <div class="cam-why__climate-item">
          <span class="cam-why__climate-num">88°F</span>
          <span class="cam-why__climate-label"><a href="https://www.weather-us.com/en/new-jersey-usa/camden-climate" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#7CB342">Avg summer high in Camden</a></span>
