<!-- ══ RESIDENTIAL ══ -->
<section class="cam-res">
  <div class="cam-res__container">

    <div class="cam-res__header">
      <div class="eyebrow-modern">Residential Window Film</div>
      <h2 class="cam-res__headline">Window Film for Camden Homes</h2>
      <p class="cam-res__intro">From Cramer Hill rowhouses to Cherry Hill colonials, we install window film across every type of residential property in the Camden area — matched to the building, the orientation, and what you’re trying to solve.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 1: Rowhouses -->
    <div class="res-row">
      <div class="res-row__image">
        <img src="/images/window-film-camden-nj-residential-rowhouses.jpg" alt="Brick rowhouses in a Camden NJ neighborhood — solar control and security window film for South Jersey row homes" width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="res-row__text">
        <div class="eyebrow-modern res-row__eyebrow">Rowhouses &amp; Twin Homes</div>
        <h3 class="res-row__title">The most common home in Camden — and one of the most exposed</h3>
        <p class="res-row__body">Camden’s rowhouses and twin homes are built tight to the street with large front-facing windows that take the full force of afternoon sun. South- and west-facing glass on homes in Cramer Hill, Parkside, and Whitman Park can push indoor temperatures up by 15–20°F on summer afternoons — making solar control film one of the most practical upgrades a Camden homeowner can make.</p>
        <p class="res-row__body">Security window film is also one of our most requested installs for Camden row homes. A thick security film holds glass together on impact, significantly slowing smash-and-grab entry and protecting occupants from shattered glass during break-ins or severe weather.</p>
        <ul class="res-row__bullets">
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Solar control film reduces afternoon heat gain by up to 78%</li>
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Security film holds glass together on impact — no shards, slower forced entry</li>
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Blocks 99% of UV rays — protects hardwood floors, furniture, and paint from fading</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/contact/" class="res-row__cta">Get a free rowhouse estimate →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 2: Single-family (reversed) -->
    <div class="res-row res-row--reversed">
      <div class="res-row__image">
        <img src="/images/window-film-camden-nj-residential-single-family.jpg" alt="Suburban colonial home in Cherry Hill New Jersey — energy-saving and UV-blocking window film for South Jersey single-family homes" width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="res-row__text">
        <div class="eyebrow-modern res-row__eyebrow">Single-Family Homes</div>
        <h3 class="res-row__title">Cherry Hill, Collingswood, Haddonfield, and beyond</h3>
        <p class="res-row__body">Single-family homes across Camden County — from the colonials of Cherry Hill to the Victorians of Haddonfield — often have large picture windows, skylights, and sunrooms that generate substantial solar heat gain in summer. South Jersey’s humid climate amplifies the discomfort, turning rooms with untreated west-facing glass into unusable spaces from June through September.</p>
        <p class="res-row__body">Energy-saving solar control or Low-E window film addresses the heat without replacement, renovation, or loss of natural light. UV-blocking film also prevents the fading of hardwood floors, Persian rugs, and upholstery — all common in the older homes throughout the area.</p>
        <ul class="res-row__bullets">
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Works on picture windows, skylights, sliding glass doors, and bay windows</li>
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Low-E film improves year-round comfort — cooler in summer, warmer in winter</li>
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Lifetime manufacturer warranty on all residential installations</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/contact/" class="res-row__cta">Get a free home assessment →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 3: Condos & apartments -->
    <div class="res-row">
      <div class="res-row__image">
        <img src="/images/window-film-camden-nj-residential-condo.jpg" alt="Modern waterfront condo building in Camden NJ with floor-to-ceiling glass — privacy and solar control window film for apartments and condominiums" width="680" height="480" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="res-row__text">
        <div class="eyebrow-modern res-row__eyebrow">Condos &amp; Apartment Buildings</div>
        <h3 class="res-row__title">Floor-to-ceiling views — without the heat, glare, or privacy trade-offs</h3>
        <p class="res-row__body">Camden’s growing waterfront has brought a wave of modern condo and apartment construction with floor-to-ceiling glass — beautiful in concept but often brutal in practice. The same windows that frame Delaware River views can turn units into greenhouses by afternoon, and provide zero privacy from neighboring buildings at night.</p>
        <p class="res-row__body">Window film solves all three problems at once. Spectrally selective solar film cuts heat and glare while preserving the view. Frosted or decorative film adds privacy in bathrooms or bedrooms without blocking light. We work with building management and HOA boards on specifications and ensure all films meet condo association requirements before installation begins.</p>
        <ul class="res-row__bullets">
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Spectrally selective film preserves river views while cutting heat by up to 55%</li>
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Frosted and decorative film for privacy in bedrooms and bathrooms</li>
          <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>HOA and building management coordination included with every condo project</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/contact/" class="res-row__cta">Get a condo or apartment estimate →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

